11) Days payable outstanding

We will now have a look at our accounts payable, or creditors, and a ratio called the Days Payable Outstanding (DPO). This ratio is an efficiency ratio that measures the average number of days a company takes to pay its suppliers.
The DPO ratio is calculated as follows:
Days Payable Outstanding = (Ending Balance Creditors / Total COGS) * Days in Financial Year

